mapping "E700X.1" source="E700X" target="68528007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target quality=100 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source E700X SNOMED CT 68528007 is the Swedish unspecified (UNS) code for hyperphenylalaninemia due
        to PAH deficiency, sitting under WHO ICD-10 E70.0 Classical phenylketonuria (which Athena maps
        to SNOMED CT 432872 concept_code 7573000). Because the source is deliberately UNS and spans the
        E70.0/E70.1 BH4-deficiency group, the broader SNOMED CT 4287416 (concept_code 68528007) — the WHO
        E70.1 crosswalk target — is the best standard concept: it subsumes all PAH- and BH4-related
        hyperphenylalaninemias without forcing a more specific child. high: legitimate one-level broader
        map with crosswalk-verified ancestor.
        """
}
